Subject: [PATCH] topology: reconcile the reported native backhaul STA VAP

A successful native handover reported the new parent in its second topology
response before the verification deadline. The vendor-BSS receive path still
appended a second station-mode row, retaining the enabled previous parent.
The controller selected that obsolete first row and discarded correctly
correlated metrics against the wrong parent epoch.

Apply the existing single-backhaul-STA-per-radio invariant directly to this
receive path, before parent selection. Preserve APs, other radios and unrelated
STA modes. Stage the bounded snapshot so truncated, ambiguous or oversized
reports do not partially mutate the live model. Copy complete BSS information
values instead of the legacy partial dm_bss_t assignment operator, preserving
load and metric fields when records move. Propagate malformed payloads
and pass the TLV length in host order. No steering deadline is extended and
success responses do not substitute for observed topology or fresh metrics.

Upstream-Status: Pending

